to be released in December this year Tom  Clancy's The Division compromised as the  sequel to The recruited novel released  earlier this year I was fortunate enough  to get my hands on a review copy and  after reading through it twice I'm going  to give my own spoiler-free review  however if you haven't read recruited  and you're planning to I suggest  switching off the video now I won't be  talking about everything that happened  but there will certainly be some parts  that'll cover that could be considered  as spoilers I'll put a link to my review  of recruited in the description  otherwise let's get into it  foreign  [Music]  right off the bat you can tell that  compromise has been written in a way  that doesn't require you to have any  prior experience in the series you can  pick this up as a standalone novel and  comfortably follow what's going on  however in saying that I would fully  recommend reading recruited first as  this really sets the scene with what  happens in compromised and having a  deeper understanding of what these  characters have been through up until  this point  as a quick recap of recruiters located  in Maryland Myra kanhai is a cyber  security expert who previously served in  the U.S Navy when things started getting  bad she rushed over to the enlistment  officers so she could do her part in  helping bring the situation back under  control but when she got there she  realized it was too late  the building was dark all she found was  a man in an officer's uniform slumped  over the disc  he'd clearly taken his own life rather  than succumbed to the virus that was  ravaging the country  it was at this point that Myra knew that  all she could do was to fall back and  write out the situation at hand to do  her best to ensure that she and her  younger brother could survive  they would go on to move around from  building to building District to  District in search of a safe place they  could call home  eventually they would join a community  of survivors called Athena  in time Myers passed in the Navy would  become known a much to her objection to  the idea she was placed in charge of  Athena's security protecting it from the  Scavengers and hostile groups who only  wanted to take advantage of what was  going on  unfortunately Mara's time of hit a  security led her to making some tough  decisions some of these decisions  required action for the survival of the  community but would ultimately lead to  the death of members including her own  brother  this would lead to Athena community  members screaming out and placing the  blame on her for everything that went  wrong  speaking of unwanted distracting noise  does your house sound a little something  like this  have you had to listen to Peppa Pig for  the 400th time this week  the big tummy daddy well maybe you just  want a little bit of me time to enjoy  the latest episode of Love Island well  look no further than the Logitech G Pro  X headset in all seriousness my friends  at Logitech sent me through a pier last  week and so far I'm very impressed with  them they're extremely comfortable and  I'm legitimately hearing more in the way  of in-game background sounds than I've  heard previously plus their  compatibility with the G hug companion  software allows for more customization  options to suit your particular  environment no matter how intrusive it  can be  basically they do a bloody good job of  blocking out the stuff you don't want to  hear and provide an immersive enough  experience to ignore the chaos that is  unfolding around you Logitech also sent  me through a stream cam so on my other  Channel that I have really talked about  yet you'll be able to see my exhausted  three hours of sleep a night face in  full HD and 60 frames per second kids  are great really  but otherwise a big thank you to  Logitech for sponsoring the video and  for helping me keep some of my sanity  anyway where were we right Myra kanhai  collapse of society Athena head of  security responsible for her brother's  death  one day Athena would come under attack  from a large group of hyenas Myra knew  this day could come and had prepared the  community the best she could but the  sheer number of hyenas was just too much  fortunately for Athena there happened to  be some division agents operating in the  area just in time they came to their aid  and repelled the attackers but would  unfortunately lose one of their own in  the battle  after the outbreak the traditional way  of recruiting division agents has long  since passed new recruits are now found  out in the field and thrown into the  deep end  after seeing what Myra had attempted to  do for the settlement the most senior  agent Brenda saw something in her and  would accept her into their cell  Myra Brenda and Leo would continue on  with their original Mission before they  came across Athena to assist the I-10  Fleet of truckies who were doing their  best to provide the much needed supplies  to the settlements on the Eastern  seaboard  the agents would learn of their Northern  counterparts the Romans a vicious Armada  of Raiders and bandits  but while engaging this hostile group  they would also learn of a rogue agent  with the new ranks who had a grudge to  settle with the division  following on from their last mission and  recruited the team have been left  bruised and bettered compromise begins  several months after these events while  their physical wounds have more or less  healed the potential psychological scars  aren't quite so easy to see or manage  after their first major mission and all  of the events that led up to it Myra  kanhai is no longer the green recruit  she once was  he still carries the Survivor guilt that  has plagued her since the loss of her  brother and countless others she has  tried to help  this isn't just a story of how they all  tackle their next mission but how  they'll deal with the emotional damage  that has been inflicted on the team  since each of them were first activated  while their previous success over the  Romans brings hope to the damaged Nation  it isn't long before Myra and uselle are  made aware of a group of environmental  extremists who are dead set on helping  the world repair  their first targets Texan oil refineries  they want to see a world free from  fossil fuels the fuels that are also  helping the Truckee Supply the various  settlements of survivors with food and  supplies  after being dispatched they would also  learn of a new private military company  who were acting as the saviors but also  the overlords of these vulnerable  communities  with very different goals in mind these  new factions are a time bomb waiting to  explode and the agents are caught right  in the middle  sequels can often leave a bitter taste  especially if one really enjoyed the  first in the series but I'm happy to  announce that this certainly isn't the  case with compromised if anything I'm  going to say that this is a step up from  recruited and I'll explain why soon  anyone who watched my review on  recruited or even just looked at the  back cover of the book will know that  I'm a fan of Thomas parrott's writing  style but the expectations on a sequel  are always substantially higher it isn't  enough to be just as good as the  original  compromised story flow is relatively  similar to recruited but it felt a  deeper connection to the facilities the  agents were visiting and staying in the  factions originally felt like that they  were just reskinned versions of what  we've already seen in the division  universe but ended up playing out much  differently than what was expected  the relationships between agents  admittedly didn't feel quite the same as  recruited but some of the other  characters were certainly more memorable  I don't think I would call this a  negative but I definitely missed a  little bit of the Sass and the playful  banter that one character in particular  brought in the first novel  one thing that I felt very early on is  that Thomas seems to be finding his  stride in the division Universe now I  feel like he had a bit of fun with this  one  the twists and turns while still present  and recruited were on another tier with  compromised but the reason I really  enjoyed this is a die-hard fan of the  franchise story is that compromise  wasn't just borrowing the division  setting but that there were a couple of  instances that really tied it together  with the story that we all know and love  from the games  I mean the ending there it's  disappointing that a current or won't  talk about it for a little while because  [ __ ] is starting to get interesting up  in here  sorry April calendar I'm going to be  looking out for other Echoes In the game  from here on  if you're a fan of the division story I  see this much light recruited as a must  read  Thomas does a fantastic job of building  a world that has become an everyday  fight for survival the characters are  well articulated to the point of forming  an emotional bond with them and the  action scenes literally had my heart  rate increase while I attempted to read  at the same Pace I imagine the events  were playing out  both novels complement the universe in a  way that the games couldn't video games  need to appeal to an audience in a  different way so it's often the case  that the story suffers to a certain  extent  these novels really flesh out what it's  like living in this world they also add  a more human feel to the division agents  showing their flaws the stuff they have  to go through the damage they take the  way shd Tech works the depth and  repercussions of the decisions they have  to make on the Fly  I'm going to say that my only complaint  is that I have to wait for the next one  in the series and for the game storyline  to catch up to the novels  you can pre-order compromise now I'll  leave a link in the description I'm  actually really looking forward to this  and we'll be happily adding this to my  collection although I admit I still  haven't pushed myself a physical copy of  recruited yet so I should probably get  onto that now anyway I hope you found  this useful I've certainly enjoyed it  and look forward to eventually being  able to talk about what has been  discovered in Myra's Journey thanks for  watching and I'll catch you in the next  one cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  thank you
 

